# Normalise line endings in the repository so editing on the Windows gaming
# PC doesn't rewrite every file. A single session that flipped the tree to
# CRLF turned a 1,600 line change into a 3,900 line diff and reset git blame
# for the whole project.
#
# Rule: LF in the repo for everything, and check out CRLF only for the files
# Windows genuinely needs it for.

* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe is the one thing that actually requires CRLF -- a .bat with LF
# endings can mis-parse multi-line blocks.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# PowerShell handles LF fine, but these sit next to the .bat files and get
# opened in Notepad by people debugging a failed install.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# AC reads these itself; keep them in the form the game and Content Manager
# write them.
*.ini text eol=crlf

*.png binary
*.dds binary
*.acd binary
